@startuml
' Source: motaa-app/MASTER_REVERSE_ENGINEERING.md §7 + approved research priorities
title How to prove an algorithm is correct
caption TEST STRATEGY · Planned workflow, not completed parity testing
skinparam backgroundColor #FAF8F0
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFEF9
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #756020
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #E8DDAF
skinparam ArrowColor #756020
start
:Identify source algorithm + confidence;
:Choose fixed input / settings / ephemeris version;
:Run original APK and capture reference output;
:Run independent new implementation;
:Normalize units, time zones\nand rounding for comparison;
if (Within field-specific tolerance?) then (Yes)
  :Store golden fixture and pass;
else (No)
  :Classify difference: source assumption,\nephemeris version, calendar, or formatting;
  :Fix discrepancy and rerun;
endif
:Test boundaries: reform, era years,\nNakshatras, cusps, retrograde stations,\nhouse systems and Rahu variants;
if (All mandatory test gates pass?) then (Yes)
  :Eligible for verified-parity claim;
else (No)
  :Keep unsupported/unverified label;
endif
stop
@enduml
